 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "Regular -er verbs",
   "body": "Most French verbs end in **-er** in the infinitive: *parler* (to speak), *habiter* (to live), *travailler* (to work), *aimer* (to like, to love). They all follow one pattern. Take off **-er** and add the endings:\n\nThe great news for speaking: *parle, parles, parle, parlent* all sound **the same** — the endings **-e, -es, -e, -ent** are silent. Only *nous parlons* and *vous parlez* sound different. (Never pronounce the **-ent** of *ils parlent*!)",
   "table": {
    "head": [
     "Pronoun",
